  At a fixed alert budget the better RANKER wins. A signal that only
  matches 'random' is carrying no information about the outcome.
  WATCH THE TIGHTEST BUDGETS. A real ranker is BEST at the top; a signal
  that only wins at loose budgets and collapses at 1-2% is over-scaling
  its extreme predictions, not ranking well.

  Bootstrap over events (2000 resamples, alert budget 71):
    lift            5th 0.21x   median 1.00x   95th 4.00x
    precision diff  5th -11.3pp  median +0.0pp  95th +8.5pp
    model beats stale in 43.5% of resamples
    -> lift interval INCLUDES 1.0. Not yet distinguishable from chance
       at this sample size; extend the window before claiming it.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  events     = both rungs quoted at t, model read BOTH (each hidden in some pass),
               and the pair repriced by t+h so the outcome is adjudicated
  confirmed  = fresh prices at t+h still show a violation
  base rate  = what you get by alerting at random. The floor.
  stale prec = precision of the ARITHMETIC rule on stale prints at t
  model prec = precision of the MODEL's estimated gap, at the SAME alert count
  lift       = model precision / stale precision. >1 means the model
               identifies real arbitrage that arithmetic cannot see.

  VERDICT: the model wins at only 1 of 5 horizons -- not
  a stable effect. Treat as suggestive, extend the test window before claiming.
